Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.26,0:03:07.55,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Tsukishiro?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.23,0:03:11.21,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,It's my first time here at the school.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.61,0:03:13.71,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,Which way to the teachers' office?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.85,0:03:18.74,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Our new acting chairman has a \Nterrible sense of direction, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.93,0:03:22.63,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,And here I thought you'd spotted \Nus on the surveillance cameras
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.63,0:03:25.02,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,and came to meet us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.41,0:03:28.02,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,What an amusing theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.02,0:03:31.79,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,The building that houses \Nthe teachers' office is—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.65,0:03:44.84,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,From the rumors, I expected more \Nfrom you, Ayanokoji Kiyotaka-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.05,0:03:49.04,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,That was quite aggressive of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.31,0:03:54.00,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,Weren't you the one issuing \Norders to get him expelled?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.68,0:03:58.53,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Since the school's top brass \Nrefuses to openly expel someone,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.09,0:04:03.64,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,it's understandable that you'd want \Nto act through someone like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.01,0:04:05.63,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,But don't you think
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.63,0:04:09.34,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,our acting chairman resorting to \Nopen assault might cause problems?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.34,0:04:11.01,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.65,0:04:15.40,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,I've swapped a dummy video \Ninto the security camera.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.55,0:04:18.86,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,A message from your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.16,0:04:25.68,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,"I refuse to play along with \Nthese childish games any longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.36,0:04:27.88,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,Return at once."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.75,0:04:31.03,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,If your answer is yes, blink twice.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.74,0:04:39.78,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,No intention to voluntarily leave school?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.25,0:04:54.60,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,My position at this school will \Nbe official beginning in April.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.97,0:04:56.36,Main,Tsukishiro,0,0,0,,Look forward to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.92,0:05:06.24,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Not fighting back was a wise choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.66,0:05:09.83,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You never know how the footage might be used.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.83,0:05:11.72,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,More importantly, Sakayanagi...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.45,0:05:16.09,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Would you like to officially \Ncompete on the upcoming exam?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.21,0:05:21.59,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I wasn't expecting you to \Nbe the one to propose it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.12,0:05:25.10,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If he's going to start meddling in April,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.10,0:05:29.27,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'd like to make our standing \Nclear and be done with it first.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.27,0:05:33.52,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Yes. I'll gladly face you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.99,0:05:46.83,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,I will now explain the final \Nspecial exam of this school year.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.87,0:05:50.31,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Your combined might will be \Nput to the test in an exam
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.31,0:05:52.25,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,based off of subjects of your choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.68,0:05:56.58,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,As in the paper shuffle, \Nyou'll face off against another class.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.68,0:06:01.79,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,First, you'll choose any ten \Nsubjects you like for the exam.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.64,0:06:07.44,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,If there are any questions, \Nfeel free to ask, Ike.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.40,0:06:09.88,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,B-But...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.88,0:06:13.83,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,You're not gonna get mad \Nat me for interrupting?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.83,0:06:18.98,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,I start to get nervous if I don't hear \None of your pointless interruptions.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.98,0:06:22.65,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Then... could it be \Nrock-paper-scissors or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.65,0:06:24.08,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,No way, man!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.08,0:06:25.74,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Let's assume rock-paper-scissors \Nis one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.18,0:06:27.37,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Seriously?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.73,0:06:28.84,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.37,0:06:32.06,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The only points of caution:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.06,0:06:34.42,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,No duplicated subjects.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.95,0:06:39.36,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,No subjects that might present \Ndifficulties with facilities,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.36,0:06:41.69,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,seasons, or number of people.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.69,0:06:43.83,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Nothing too obscure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.94,0:06:43.54,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(525,325)\pos(148,40)}Beer Pong
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.94,0:06:43.54,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(525,325)\pos(262,40)}Roundnet
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.94,0:06:43.54,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(525,325)\pos(378,40)}Kronum
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.94,0:06:43.54,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(525,325)\pos(492,40)}Padel
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.08,0:06:43.54,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(525,325)\pos(148,204)}Hurling
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.08,0:06:43.54,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(525,325)\pos(262,204)}Dacau
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.08,0:06:43.54,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(525,325)\pos(378,204)}Jai Alai
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.08,0:06:43.54,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(525,325)\pos(492,204)\q2}Wood Cobra
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.19,0:06:47.16,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Academic subjects must be \Npart of the curriculum,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.94,0:06:50.86,sign_9637_92_Beer_Pong_,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,300)\q2\move(320,50,192,50,1843,2342)\an8}Language {\t(467,507,1 \alpha&HFF&)}Math {\alpha&H00&}English {\t(632,674,1 \alpha&HFF&)}Social Studies\N{\alpha&H00&\t(800,841,1 \alpha&HFF&)}History {\alpha&H00&\t(967,1008,1 \alpha&HFF&)}Biology {\alpha&H00&}Chemistry {\t(1134,1175,1 \alpha&HFF&)}Physics
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.16,0:06:49.70,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,and the school will write the questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.16,0:06:52.00,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,You're free to decide the rules yourselves,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.00,0:06:54.68,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,but they must not allow for ties.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.53,0:06:58.83,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Your opposing class will \Nalso submit ten subjects
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.83,0:07:00.65,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,for a total of twenty subjects.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.05,0:07:03.19,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,We're doing twenty subjects?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.19,0:07:04.90,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,That's way too many!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.90,0:07:06.20,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.56,0:07:11.69,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,On the day of the test, each class will \Nchoose five subjects out of the ten offered.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.20,0:07:14.94,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,So the other five are like a bluff?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.94,0:07:15.66,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.94,0:07:18.07,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The actual test will consist \Nof seven subjects.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.63,0:07:22.67,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The school will choose one \Nat random for each round.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.67,0:07:26.35,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,You won't be told what the next subject is,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.35,0:07:28.12,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,and once a student has participated,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.12,0:07:31.18,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,they can't participate \Nagain until everyone has.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.18,0:07:33.96,Main,Sato,0,0,0,,My head is spinning with \Nall this information...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.96,0:07:37.02,Main,Sakura,0,0,0,,So... that means...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.40,0:07:39.90,Main,Kushida,0,0,0,,Out of all the subjects \Nwe submit to each other,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.90,0:07:43.61,Main,Kushida,0,0,0,,we only compete in seven of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.61,0:07:45.40,Main,Sato,0,0,0,,Oh, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.67,0:07:48.75,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,And the most important rule
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.75,0:07:50.56,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,is the existence of a team captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.22,0:07:55.47,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The student chosen as captain can't \Nparticipate in any of the subjects,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.47,0:07:58.31,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,but they can be involved in all subjects,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.31,0:08:00.66,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,and will receive bonus \Npoints if their class wins.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.02,0:08:03.17,Main,Hasebe,0,0,0,,And if their class loses?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.79,0:08:08.38,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The captain will be expelled immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.44,0:08:11.85,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Not again!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.08,0:08:16.79,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,After class, the captain will take part \Nin a lottery to pick your opponent.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.79,0:08:18.40,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,You can select anyone you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.11,0:08:20.41,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Talk it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.12,0:08:24.87,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0\c&H132934&\fs18\fay.4\fax-.8\pos(212,22)}Final Special Exam Overview and Strategy Meeting
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.12,0:08:24.87,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0\c&H132934&\fs13\fay.4\fax-.8\pos(260,176)}*These materials must be returned after the meeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.32,0:08:27.36,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Where'd Koenji go?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.68,0:08:30.82,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,That bastard's messing around again!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.82,0:08:32.95,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Getting angry won't solve anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.18,0:08:35.66,Main,Mori,0,0,0,,Hey, where'd Hirata-kun go?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.66,0:08:36.95,Main,Inogashira,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.95,0:08:39.41,Main,Inogashira,0,0,0,,He knew we were getting \Ntogether after class...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.41,0:08:44.17,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Hirata-kun remains useless, \Nso I suppose I'll have to do it myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.82,0:08:49.55,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,I, um... I'm going to the bathroom!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.55,0:08:50.68,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,I'll be back soon!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.07,0:08:53.18,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.60,0:08:56.92,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,There's one thing I wanna \Nget clear before we talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.92,0:08:57.81,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.29,0:09:02.50,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,There are a lot of people who don't \Nlike how the last test turned out.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.50,0:09:03.99,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Right, Kanji?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.99,0:09:08.88,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,I guess it's more like... I don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.88,0:09:13.00,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Why'd Ayanokoji place first in the vote?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.80,0:09:16.39,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Allow me to explain.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.39,0:09:18.07,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I have a theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.07,0:09:19.12,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Hold it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.12,0:09:22.57,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,We want the explanation from Ayanokoji.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.57,0:09:25.38,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Our buddy's gone, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.60,0:09:28.38,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Sorry. I don't know, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.38,0:09:30.47,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Don't give me that crap!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.47,0:09:33.51,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I don't think Ayanokoji-kun knows the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.51,0:09:35.68,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,It was out of his control.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.68,0:09:37.52,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Out of his control?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.52,0:09:39.04,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.40,0:09:42.09,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Remember what Yamauchi-kun said?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.04,0:09:44.44,Flashback,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,That's it. Sakayanagi!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.44,0:09:46.40,Flashback,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,Go talk to Sakayanagi!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.40,0:09:48.57,Flashback,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,She said she'd give me their positive votes!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.57,0:09:51.08,Flashback,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,How could she betray me like this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.52,0:09:55.34,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,She made him think she'd \Nmade a secret pact with him
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.34,0:09:58.33,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,to destroy Ayanokoji-kun, then betrayed him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.33,0:10:01.33,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,So why choose Ayanokoji?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.57,0:10:03.55,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,He's a neutral entity.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.55,0:10:05.92,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,The protection point will \Nbe irrelevant with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.92,0:10:08.71,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'm sure anyone else would \Nhave worked just as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.71,0:10:11.68,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,But... that's just you guessing!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.68,0:10:13.64,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,That's right. It's an inference.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.86,0:10:19.72,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,But if you want to be angry at someone, \Nbe angry at me, not him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.72,0:10:24.27,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'm the primary reason \NYamauchi-kun was expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.54,0:10:26.10,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Okay, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.02,0:10:32.90,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Is it okay if I volunteer to be \Ncaptain for this special exam?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.24,0:10:37.35,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's true that I've lost \Nsome of the class's trust.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.72,0:10:42.41,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Therefore, I want to clear the \Nsuspicions by becoming a sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.41,0:10:43.71,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Ayanokoji...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.71,0:10:45.08,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Sounds good to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.08,0:10:47.58,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Then no one'll have to be expelled!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.58,0:10:49.48,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,Hey, hang on a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.48,0:10:52.92,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,That makes it sound like we're \Ngoing to throw the challenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.19,0:10:57.05,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,Do we really want to fight some other \Nclass under Ayanokoji-kun's leadership?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.05,0:11:00.31,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,Shouldn't we consider other candidates?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.68,0:11:06.70,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I don't think anyone here wants \Nto run the risk of being expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.70,0:11:08.69,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Myself included.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.69,0:11:10.65,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,That's true, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.65,0:11:14.32,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,And since he's got the protection point, \Nhe's perfect for the job, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.70,0:11:20.94,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Even if he is the captain, others can \Nconsult with him on planning beforehand.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.36,0:11:23.92,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,It doesn't particularly \Nmatter who plays the role.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.70,0:11:28.51,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Horikita's pushing hard for \Nme in the captain role.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.85,0:11:32.52,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,And I doubt anyone will object.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.52,0:11:34.32,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Are there any objections?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.17,0:11:42.67,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Will you take it on, then, Ayanokoji-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.27,0:11:44.22,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.10,0:11:55.26,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,As expected, every class chose their \Nprotection point holder as captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.05,0:11:59.86,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,Starting with Class A, \Neach of you will draw one lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.86,0:12:05.29,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,The class that draws the marked paper will \Nhave the right to choose their opponent.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.99,0:12:09.13,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,As they say, "Good things are found \Nin what others leave behind."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.13,0:12:11.33,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I shall draw last.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.64,0:12:13.30,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Please proceed, Ichinose-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.56,0:12:15.30,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Don't mind if I do!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.30,0:12:17.13,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,1200)\c&H505961&\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs12\bord0\shad0\frx40\frz37.35\pos(333.333,208.667)}Tokyo Metropolitan Advanced\NNurturing High School
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.54,0:12:22.55,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Oh, too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.57,0:12:26.31,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(225,0)\c&H3C454D&\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs10\bord0\shad0\frz5.573\pos(281.334,332)}Tokyo Metropolitan Advanced\NNurturing High School
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.57,0:12:26.31,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(225,0)\c&H2C3339&\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs10\bord0\shad0\frz14.93\pos(438,283.334)}Acting Chairman\NTsukishiro
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.57,0:12:26.31,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(225,0)\c&H2C3339&\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs14\bord2\shad0\pos(313.333,105.333)\frz6.308\3c&HE2EAEE&}Right to Choose\NOpposing Class
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.31,0:12:27.81,Main,Kaneda,0,0,0,,It's a winner.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.16,0:12:33.23,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,It seems there's no need to check \Nthe final paper, Mr. Mashima.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.23,0:12:34.29,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.76,0:12:38.74,Main,Mashima,0,0,0,,Kaneda, tell us which class you'd like to face.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.01,0:12:42.58,Main,Kaneda,0,0,0,,Class D wants to face Class B.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.58,0:12:45.12,Main,Ichinose,0,0,0,,Sounds good to me. No holding back, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.52,0:12:49.12,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I had assumed you'd target Class C.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.12,0:12:51.08,Main,Kaneda,0,0,0,,One route to a comeback would be to
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.08,0:12:54.52,Main,Kaneda,0,0,0,,go after the points of as \Nhigh a class as possible,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.52,0:12:58.13,Main,Kaneda,0,0,0,,but I'd like to avoid facing Class A for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.49,0:13:00.09,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.09,0:13:02.51,Main,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,Best of luck to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.17,0:13:05.07,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,This result was predetermined.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.92,0:13:10.45,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I arranged it with Ichinose \Nand Ishizaki in advance...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.52,0:13:13.52,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,300)\fs14\c&HAEAF9A&\3c&HE0E0CE&\shad0\pos(344.667,190.667)}Ishizaki Daichi
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.52,0:13:13.52,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,300)\fs14\an1\c&HEFE9E7&\3c&HF8F8F8&\shad0\pos(306,219)}Ayanokoji Kiyotaka
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.52,0:13:13.52,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,300)\fs14\an1\c&HEFE9E7&\3c&HF8F8F8&\shad0\pos(282.,249)}(No Subject)
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.52,0:13:13.52,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,300)\c&HD7D2CB&\bord0\shad0\fs12\pos(192,288)\an7}Got it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.86,0:13:19.01,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,to make sure they'd let us fight Class A.
