Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.36,0:13:28.97,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,That's all for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.44,0:13:31.77,Main,Class C,0,0,0,,It's over!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.91,0:13:40.13,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Hirata-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.06,0:13:42.80,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Can I talk to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.29,0:13:45.29,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Could you please leave me alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.29,0:13:46.18,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.18,0:13:47.85,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Just go away!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.48,0:13:54.47,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,B-But I...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.82,0:13:58.32,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,I'm just worried about you, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.32,0:14:01.02,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,You have no reason to worry about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.70,0:14:03.53,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Hey, Yosuke-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.53,0:14:06.29,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Don't you think that's going a little too far?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.87,0:14:09.94,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Don't call me by my given \Nname like we're friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.38,0:14:12.54,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,We're not seeing each other anymore, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.79,0:14:14.22,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Fine, Hirata-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.22,0:14:16.19,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,You're being way too hard on Mii-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.19,0:14:18.79,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,I'm just acting how you usually do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.57,0:14:21.67,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,I-I'm doing it for the class!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.89,0:14:24.36,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Just shut up, would you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.36,0:14:25.68,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,If you don't...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.04,0:14:27.49,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,You know what'll happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.47,0:14:41.73,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,Wait, Hirata-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.10,0:14:48.56,Main,Horikawa,0,0,0,,No one can help Hirata-kun right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.56,0:14:50.94,Main,Horikawa,0,0,0,,Focus on the conversation in front of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.72,0:14:55.37,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Surprised to see you stayed today, Koenji.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.81,0:14:59.71,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,The Horikita girl practically begged me to.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.21,0:15:06.07,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,That said, I hope today will \Nbe the start and end of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.07,0:15:08.09,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,I'm a busy man, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.31,0:15:10.19,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'll make it short, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.19,0:15:11.06,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Before the next class,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.06,0:15:15.60,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I want you all to submit a subject \Nyou feel utmost confidence in.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.91,0:15:17.34,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.34,0:15:22.11,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,"Now that you're in the discussion, \Nyou'd better meet your quota," eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.44,0:15:25.41,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'm sure you have at least one \Nespecially strong subject.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.41,0:15:28.82,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Or will you willfully turn \Nthe class against you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.56,0:15:34.21,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Get it out of your head that \Nsuch words might sway me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.21,0:15:38.08,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,It's true that I'm an unparalleled genius,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.32,0:15:43.59,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,but I'm the one who decides whether \Nor not I use that genius for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.16,0:15:48.22,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Unparalleled genius, my ass.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.53,0:15:51.50,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I'll speak with Koenji-kun later.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.50,0:15:53.31,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,For now, let's see what happens.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.48,0:16:03.78,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Heya.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.85,0:16:08.70,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Rare for you to invite me to your place.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.64,0:16:11.75,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,If anyone were to see us...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.39,0:16:15.54,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Um... wouldn't it be a problem?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.54,0:16:18.92,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's growing less necessary that we hide.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.01,0:16:24.88,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Feels like our relationship is \Nbecoming more and more open, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.38,0:16:26.72,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Is that okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.06,0:16:28.89,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's not an issue at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.89,0:16:32.52,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I want inside information on the class, \Nincluding what's going on with Hirata.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.52,0:16:36.35,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,And we have to meet in person for that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.35,0:16:40.35,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,There are some things one can \Nbest learn by meeting in person.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.04,0:16:43.48,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But first...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.10,0:16:52.35,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's your birthday, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.40,0:16:55.31,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,You learned my birthday?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.70,0:16:57.37,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Hey, can I look inside?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.37,0:16:58.28,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.16,0:17:03.69,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,A necklace?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.13,0:17:06.35,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,And it's a heart?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.77,0:17:09.76,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Is this really a gift for a friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.41,0:17:12.78,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Wasn't it expensive?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.78,0:17:16.01,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It wasn't cheap. Approximately 20,000.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.01,0:17:17.26,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,That's a lot!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.26,0:17:23.60,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It was number one on the site's list of \N"best presents for high school girls."
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.60,0:17:28.03,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,I know you're smart, \Nbut you're kinda dumb in that area.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.23,0:17:29.60,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Am I?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.60,0:17:33.66,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,When you buy accessories for a girl, \Nyou're supposed to pick them out yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.91,0:17:38.04,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,Honestly, this is pretty \Nmuch a 10 out of 100.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.30,0:17:40.60,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Would a box of cakes have been better?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.32,0:17:43.29,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,That would've been a 15.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.83,0:17:48.08,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,You got a mirror?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.08,0:17:49.75,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Do you think that I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.09,0:17:54.57,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,I thought so.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.57,0:17:57.60,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,A heart's a bit childish.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.00,0:18:00.51,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If you don't like it, you can leave it here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.51,0:18:05.72,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,But I'm gorgeous to start with, so pretty \Nmuch anything looks good on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.17,0:18:10.40,Main,Karuizawa,0,0,0,,I suppose I might as well keep it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.40,0:18:12.92,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Feel free to, if you'd like.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.86,0:18:23.60,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\c&HB4917E&\3c&HCCBBAA&\fs20\shad0}Pedestrians and Bicycles Only
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.81,0:18:27.11,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,You're out early.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.11,0:18:29.63,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I had some business at the library.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.06,0:18:34.02,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,Oh? Is the special exam proceeding well?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.33,0:18:37.39,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Your sister is certainly raring for a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.66,0:18:38.74,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.30,0:18:43.13,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Regarding that, there's something \NI've been wanting to ask you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.12,0:18:46.38,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,On the day we first met,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.26,0:18:50.90,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,why did you chew her out \Nand try to drive her away?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.32,0:18:56.65,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,I was disappointed in Suzune.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.08,0:19:00.56,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,Not in her grades, but in her maturity.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.56,0:19:02.41,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Her maturity?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.62,0:19:05.80,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,When she was a child, \Nshe smiled a great deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.80,0:19:10.63,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,But now she's dependent \Non me. She imitates me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.52,0:19:16.46,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,And mimicking you is the reason \Nshe plays the ice princess?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.46,0:19:18.22,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,It's not just her attitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.22,0:19:23.12,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,What she eats, drinks... \NEven her favorite color and taste in clothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.49,0:19:26.29,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,She's brought them all in line with mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.68,0:19:28.60,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,That isn't growth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.19,0:19:31.73,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,So despite your flawless exterior,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.73,0:19:35.40,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,you failed at properly \Ncommunicating with your sister?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.78,0:19:39.66,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,There is no flawless human being. Is there?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.95,0:19:45.16,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I suppose not. \NBut she's trying to change now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.81,0:19:49.25,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,If Suzune were to stop chasing my phantom,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.25,0:19:50.89,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,cut off her dependency,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.89,0:19:55.38,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,and face herself with perfect honesty,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.03,0:20:00.93,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,then she would surpass me, and become \Nsomeone that even you could not ignore.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.60,0:20:04.43,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,But only if she's able to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.84,0:20:07.56,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I think she is changing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.28,0:20:10.12,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,No, that's not right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.78,0:20:12.96,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I think I might try changing her.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.48,0:20:17.48,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Not in the gradual ways I've \Ndone before, but genuinely.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.63,0:20:21.84,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,Oh? Interesting to hear that from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.24,0:20:24.40,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I have one other question.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.40,0:20:25.30,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.73,0:20:29.37,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Are you and Tachibana there dating?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.44,0:20:32.71,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,No, not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.43,0:20:34.48,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.00,0:20:37.16,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,Still,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.16,0:20:41.70,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,it's interesting to see such an ordinary \Nhigh school sentiment come from your mouth.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.05,0:20:45.68,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I believe I am an absolutely \Nordinary high schooler.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.97,0:20:50.73,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,Then, speaking as an ordinary high \Nschooler, have you found a girlfriend?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.73,0:20:52.84,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Not at the moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.59,0:20:56.94,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,I wouldn't mind leaving Suzune in your hands,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.52,0:21:00.29,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,but I can't quite see the \Ntwo of you together, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.29,0:21:01.66,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Of course you can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.66,0:21:03.80,Main,Tachibana,0,0,0,,D-Don't say that!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.80,0:21:06.56,Main,Tachibana,0,0,0,,You're gonna trigger a flag or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.56,0:21:07.56,Main,Manabu,0,0,0,,A flag?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.56,0:21:10.01,Main,Tachibana,0,0,0,,Oh, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.01,0:21:13.59,Main,Tachibana,0,0,0,,I mean, there's sort of a rule that \Nthat kind of thing backfires.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.59,0:21:17.05,Main,Tachibana,0,0,0,,It's pretty common to \Nsee two people you think
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.50,0:21:20.20,Main,Tachibana,0,0,0,,would never get together start dating...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.69,0:21:24.72,Main,Tachibana,0,0,0,,I-I mean, forget what I said.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.93,0:21:28.82,Main,Student,0,0,0,,There are too many tests!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.93,0:21:29.43,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\c&H283949&\an7\pos(20,20)\fs14\3c&HD3E4EF&\shad0\b1}Chess\NMental Math\NGo\NModern Literature
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.93,0:21:29.43,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\c&H283949&\an7\pos(340,20)\fs14\3c&HD3E4EF&\shad0\b1}Volleyball\NMath\NEnglish\NJump Rope\NDodgeball
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.49,0:21:29.43,Main,Student,0,0,0,,Class A really went for it...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.64,0:21:32.44,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,These are the subjects submitted by Class A.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.44,0:21:35.44,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,It'll be pretty hard to cover all this.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.44,0:21:36.54,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.54,0:21:39.47,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,But the same will be true for Class A.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.47,0:21:43.20,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,The key will be figuring out which \Nsubjects they're serious about.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.20,0:21:46.45,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Has anyone here ever played chess, even?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.05,0:21:48.45,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Chess...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.45,0:21:55.21,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(20,20)\c&H8C8F94&\3c&HFDFFFD&\shad0\fs10}Class A's Chosen Subjects \N\NGame Rules and Rules for the Leader\N\N・Chess\NOne player needed. Time allowance: one hour (absolute).\NRules: Standard chess rules, but more time is not granted after the 40th move.\NLeader rules: The leader can give instructions to the player at his or her discretion\Nfor, at most, 30 minutes of the allotted time.\N\N・Mental Math\NTwo players needed. Time: 30 minutes.\NRules: Students compete for speed and accuracy in calculation using an abacus.\NThe class whose participant places first wins.\NLeader rules: The leader may change one answer at his or her discretion.\N\N・Go\NThree players needed. Time allowance: one hour (absolute).\NRules: Three one-on-one matches will be conducted simultaneously.\NStandard go rules...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.03,0:21:55.21,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,In chess, the captain uses the allotted time\Nto give instructions to the players.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.41,0:22:02.22,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Which makes it possible \Nfor two captains to duel.
